rlm-pr-recent [-w|--weeks N] [-a|--author LOGIN]

List pull requests in the CURRENT repository in an fzf picker, then
jump to the one you pick. The list is every OPEN PR, however old, plus
every other PR (merged, closed) updated in the last N weeks (default
4) -- all states and all authors.

Open PRs are deliberately exempt from the date cutoff. An open PR is
unfinished work no matter how long it has been quiet, and a PR that
has gone untouched for months is the one you are most likely to have
forgotten about -- precisely the one a date filter would hide. The
cutoff exists only to bound the closed/merged tail.

Selecting a PR does one of two things, decided per PR:

  1. Its head branch is already checked out in some worktree of this
     repo -- cd there. This is also the only correct action: git
     refuses to have one branch checked out in two worktrees, so a
     checkout here would fail regardless.
  2. No worktree holds the branch -- run `gh pr checkout <N>` in the
     current worktree, switching this checkout to the PR's branch. gh
     configures tracking correctly for fork PRs too, which a plain
     `git checkout` does not.

Case 2 REFUSES when the working tree has uncommitted changes, rather
than carrying them onto the PR's branch (which is what git would do,
quietly mixing unrelated work into it). Commit or stash first, or use
rlm-pr-worktree to get a separate worktree for the PR.

Rows are `<mark> #NUM STATE AUTHOR AGE TITLE`, color-coded by state
(open green, draft grey, merged magenta, closed red).

The AUTHOR column shows `login (Real Name)` -- the name comes from
GitHub, which returns it alongside the login at no extra cost. Bots
have no name and show the bare login. Typing part of either half
finds the PR, so `marcin` reaches storytel-siudzinskim (Marcin
Siudzinski) without having to remember the handle.

The author's canonical email is also matched, though never displayed:
it is read from the mailmap (`mailmap.file`, else the repo's own
.mailmap) and keyed on the name GitHub reports. That is what lets a
plain-ascii query find a name carrying diacritics -- `siudzinski`
matches `Marcin Siudzinski` through marcin.siudzinski@storytel.com.
Authors absent from the mailmap simply lose that extra search term;
login and name still match. The mark column
is `*` when the PR's branch is checked out in the current worktree,
`>` when another worktree holds it, blank otherwise. The preview pane
shows `gh pr view` for the focused PR.

Rows are ordered by activity, newest first: the PR updated or
commented on most recently is the top row, the least recently touched
is the last. GitHub's updatedAt advances on every comment, so a PR
that only received a review comment still sorts to the top. Ordering
is by recency alone -- picking a PR does not float it up on the next
run, so the top of the list always means "newest activity" rather
than "what you last looked at".

The list is fetched live on every call (about a second for ~80 PRs)
and deliberately not cached: the state column is the reason to run
this, and a cached "open" for a PR that merged an hour ago is worse
than a one-second wait.

Related: rlm-pr-list prints a table of the PR for the branch currently
checked out across one repo or one collection dir; rlm-pr-find scans a
whole directory tree and jumps to an existing checkout. This command
starts from the repository's PRs instead, so it reaches a PR whose
branch is not on disk anywhere.

ARGUMENTS
  -w, --weeks N     How far back to look for CLOSED and MERGED PRs,
                    in weeks (default 4). Open PRs are always listed
                    regardless of age, so this does not affect them.
  -a, --author LOGIN
                    Only PRs authored by LOGIN. Omit for all authors.
  -h, --help        Print a usage line and exit.

KEYS
  Enter             Jump to the PR (cd to its worktree, or
                    check it out).
  Shift-Up/Down     Scroll the preview pane.
  Alt-Up/Down       Scroll the preview pane by half a page.
  Ctrl-T / Ctrl-E   Jump to the first / last row.
  Ctrl-P            Cycle the preview pane size (70% / 40% / hidden).
  Ctrl-G            Abort.

FILES
  ~/.cache/rlm-pr-recent/history.txt
                    Most-recently-used PRs, as <repo>:<number> lines,
                    capped at 1000. Recorded on selection but not used
                    for ordering; the picker sorts by recency alone.

REQUIRES
  gh, git, jq, fzf
